## Detailed statements and scope notes

### Q15 scope note
The theorem is about **real-linear dimension on all real inputs**. It cannot be converted into a fixed-bit storage lower bound without a precision/encoding model. The parity-pair class demonstrates the danger: identifiability depth \(n\), yet one promised-class identifier bit.

### Fixed-cut rank threshold proof across five rank notions
Let \(m=\max(p,q)\).

**Rank 1 upper bound.** A nonzero 0/1 matrix of rank one under any of the five listed notions is the indicator of a rectangle \(I\times J\). \(Q_m\) includes every complete row sum and every complete column sum. Positive row sums identify \(I\), positive column sums identify \(J\), so the matrix is recovered; the all-zero margins identify the zero matrix.

**Rank 1 lower bound.** If \(p\ge q\), take the two functions depending only on the X block that are complementary parity on X and constant over Y. Each truth matrix is \(I\times Y\), hence rank one in all five notions, and the pair agrees under every restriction fixing at most \(p-1\) coordinates. The \(q\ge p\) case is symmetric.

**Rank 2+ lower bound.** Global odd/even parity across the cut decomposes into two disjoint rectangles according to the block parities. Thus each matrix has real, nonnegative, binary-factor, GF(2), and Boolean-OR rank at most two. The complementary pair agrees through depth \(n-1\), forcing \(\kappa\ge n\). The full assignment family \(Q_n\) gives the matching upper bound.

This theorem is fixed-cut. No all-order or sign-rank claim is made.

### T3.1 exact resource formulas
Let \(s\) be the number of occurring nonzero anchor-side profiles and \(D(d,h)=\sum_{j\le h}\binom dj\).

Initial sparse fixed-width storage:
\[
S_0\le s\left[r+(p+1)D(p,k)+(q+2)D(q,k)\right]+O(n+k+r)\text{ bits}.
\]
Dense worst case:
\[
S_0\le(2^r-1)\left[(p+1)D(p,k)+(q+2)D(q,k)\right]+O(n+k+r).
\]
An affected-side update with current \(d\) free coordinates and horizon \(h\) takes
\[
U=sD(d-1,h-1)
\]
exact additions/subtractions/copies; query time is \(T=O(s)\) exact integer multiply-adds. A direct build costs
\[
O\!\left(r(2^p+2^q)+2^pD(p,k)+2^qD(q,k)+r2^rD(q,k)\right)
\]
reads/arithmetic operations in the stated construction.

These are representation-specific upper bounds, not universal lower bounds.
